An immersive interactive installation featuring a 2-meter stone-clad well structure housing an animated diorama of a submerged Galician schoolroom. The piece synthesizes folklore with mechatronic engineering, employing  lights, spatial audio, and proximity sensors to narrate the legend of an underwater village.

The art-piece was a part of the [Ollo de Vidrio](https://www.compostelacultura.gal/espectaculos/evento/ollos-de-vidro-formas-doutra-historia-de-galicia) Exhibition, curated by a Germán Labrador Méndez.

It was a collaboration with my friend and noted Spanish Philosopher, Pablo Jarauta.

The sound was designed by my talented friend, Iván Ferrer-Orozco.
